/** Every text the harness itself puts in front of a model — the system instructions, the context lines of a run's
 *  first message, the notes it appends, the refusals, the tool and parameter descriptions, the director's manual and
 *  tools — in one place, as plain constants. A text says what is true of the run it is shown in and no more: a
 *  capability it names exists, a limit it names is enforced, a state it names is the state. Placeholders are
 *  `{name}`; `text()` fills them and refuses a missing one, so no call site ships a bare placeholder. */

